forT -- SEQ 482 (Tony, 2026-10-30): FOr on the new road, PRE-REGISTERED ON TRUNK before the build.

FOr walks a field's members, binding the cursor to each in turn when the loop runs (never at build), and runs the statement
each time; break and continue land as in WHILe. This file is not run alone: pop.sh builds two inputs per row, one process each
under an alarm -- everything above this file's `stop();` (fsrc is given its three members fa fb fc by the last line), then the
row on the OLD road or on the NEW road (the rule by name, testOP on what it handed back, except FR-0, then the optional 4th
field, old-road statements after the call), then `FR NEXT` and a sentinel.

MEASURED ON THE OLD ROAD (2026-10-30), and taken as intended:
- The cursor must be DECLARED. Undeclared, the old road prints the tag `lp` per member and `*lp` prints nothing. lp is declared.
- FR-7: after the loop the cursor holds the LAST member (`print *lp` reads 3).
- FR-2 / FR-8: an empty source and a source with no list behave alike -- nothing prints, stderr reads
  `nextGroup: ERROR <source> does not contain a list`, the next statement runs. Nothing refuses.
TODAY: FOr has no action, so testOP refuses its label; FR-6's WHILe skips the inner FOr and prints 9 9; FR-7 prints 7.

FR-R (SEQ 482 R1): attributes / members (LOOPRESTRICt) is not built on the new road: FOr refuses it by name. The row uses
`attributes`: +% attaches fa fb fc as ATTRIBUTES, so on the old road `members` walks none of them (measured) and `attributes` all three.

ROWS -- id | old-road statement | new-road statement (testOP follows it, except FR-0) | after the call (optional, old road)
FR-0||it1 = FOr("for lp in fsrc; print *lp:;");|
FR-1|for lp in fsrc; print *lp:;|it1 = FOr("for lp in fsrc; print *lp:;");|
FR-2|for lp in fe; print *lp:;|it1 = FOr("for lp in fe; print *lp:;");|
FR-3|for lp in fsrc; { print *lp:; if *lp == 2; break; }|it1 = FOr("for lp in fsrc; { print *lp:; if *lp == 2; break; }");|
FR-4|for lp in fsrc; { if *lp == 2; continue; print *lp:; }|it1 = FOr("for lp in fsrc; { if *lp == 2; continue; print *lp:; }");|
FR-5|for lp in <- fsrc; print *lp:;|it1 = FOr("for lp in <- fsrc; print *lp:;");|
FR-6|while wo < 2; { wo = wo + 1; for lp in fsrc; { print *lp:; if *lp == 2; break; } print 9:; }|it1 = WHILe("while wo < 2; { wo = wo + 1; for lp in fsrc; { print *lp:; if *lp == 2; break; } print 9:; }");|
FR-7|for lp in fsrc; print *lp:; print 7:; print *lp:;|it1 = FOr("for lp in fsrc; print *lp:;");|print 7:; print *lp:;
FR-8|for lp in fn; print *lp:;|it1 = FOr("for lp in fn; print *lp:;");|
FR-R|for lp in fsrc; attributes print *lp:;|it1 = FOr("for lp in fsrc; attributes print *lp:;");|
